@page "/API"
@model ApiModel
@using Aibysitter.Rules
@using Aibysitter.Web.Linting
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "API";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Lint a rules file over HTTP: POST JSON, get findings and a score. No key, no account.";
}

<h1>API</h1>
<p>Lint a rules file over HTTP. Same rules, limits and results as the <a asp-page="/Lint">lint page</a>. No key, no account; the text is not stored or logged (<a asp-page="/Privacy">Privacy</a>).</p>
<p>To lint before each commit or after each Claude Code edit, see <a asp-page="/Hooks">Hooks</a>.</p>

<h2>Request</h2>
<p><code>POST @LintApi.Path</code> with <code>Content-Type: application/json</code>.</p>
<table class="stack">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Required</th>
            <th>Value</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><code>content</code></td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>The rules file text, at most @LintLimits.MaxContentLength.ToString("N0", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>format</code></td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>One of @string.Join(", ", Enum.GetNames<RulesFormat>()). Case-insensitive. Default <code>Auto</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>disable</code></td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>Lint rule IDs to skip, for example <code>["R004", "R013"]</code>. Their findings are not produced or scored.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<pre id="api-request"><code>POST @LintApi.Path HTTP/1.1
Host: aibysitting.net
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "# Rules\n- Always use tabs.\n- Never use tabs.\n- Use tabs because the linter expects them.",
  "format": "ClaudeMd",
  "disable": ["R004"]
}</code></pre>

<h2>Response</h2>
<pre id="api-response"><code>HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Cache-Control: no-store

{
  "rulesetVersion": @RulesetVersion.Current,
  "detectedFormat": "ClaudeMd",
  "score": 89,
  "grade": "B",
  "disabled": ["R004"],
  "findings": [
    {
      "rule": "R003",
      "line": 3,
      "severity": "Error",
      "message": "Contradicts line 2: \"use tabs\" is both required and forbidden.",
      "fixHint": "Keep one instruction and delete the other."
    },
    {
      "rule": "R001",
      "line": 4,
      "severity": "Info",
      "message": "Rationale prose: \"because\"",
      "fixHint": "Remove the explanation. State the instruction only."
    }
  ],
  "suppressed": []
}</code></pre>
<p><code>findings</code> and <code>suppressed</code> are ordered by line, then rule. <code>suppressed</code> lists findings matched by an <code>aibysitter-disable</code> comment; they are not scored. <code>rulesetVersion</code> is listed on the <a asp-page="/Rules/Changelog">changelog</a>.</p>

<h2>Errors</h2>
<p>Errors are <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457">problem details</a> (<code>application/problem+json</code>). Field errors are under <code>errors</code>, keyed by field name.</p>
<table class="stack">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Status</th>
            <th>When</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Invalid JSON; <code>content</code> missing, blank, or too long; unknown <code>format</code>; an ID in <code>disable</code> that is not a lint rule</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>413</td>
            <td>Request body over @(LintApi.MaxBodyBytes / 1024) KB</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>415</td>
            <td>Content type is not JSON</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>422</td>
            <td>Linting stopped at the 1-second pattern limit</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>429</td>
            <td>More than @Model.RateLimit.PermitLimit lint requests in @Model.RateLimit.WindowSeconds seconds from one IP address, counting lint page submissions without JavaScript and API calls together</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Browsers on other sites cannot call the API: it sends no CORS headers.</p>
